<title>CROATIA: Croatian stocks dip further in light trade.</title>
<headline>Croatian stocks dip further in light trade.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatian stocks took a further dip on Thursday in light trade as big buyers stayed away from the market.</p>
<p>* All seven traded issues fell.</p>
<p>* Volume 4,938 units, turnover 1.6 million kuna.</p>
<p>* Biggest decliner, Zagrebacka Banka E-series preference stock, plunged 70 kuna to 360 with 60 shares sold.</p>
<p>* Most actively traded, food processor Podravka, closed at 195 kuna, down five, on volume of 3,995 units.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
